# .dev.vars — local Wrangler dev secrets template (Issue #69 / ADR-0015 §9).
#
# This file is a **committed documentation template** for the local
# dev secret contract. It is NOT generated, NOT overwritten by any
# script, and NOT read at runtime. `pnpm dev` / `wrangler dev` read
# `.dev.vars` (the gitignored sibling), NOT this file. `generate-
# dev-vars` writes the gitignored `.dev.vars` only — this committed
# template stays in source control unchanged.
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Primary path: `pnpm dev`  (fileless, secrets injected from Infisical)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `pnpm dev` invokes `scripts/_run-dev.mjs`, a Windows-safe Node
# wrapper that spawns:
#
#   pnpm exec infisical run --env=dev -- pnpm exec vite dev
#
# with `shell: false` (no POSIX shell substitution) and a literal
# argv list, so secrets flow straight from Infisical into the Vite
# process. **No `.dev.vars` file is read or written** in this path.
# The CLI auto-resolves the project from the committed
# `.infisical.json` in the repo root.
#
# The injected secret set is the entire dev env of the Infisical
# project, not `wrangler.jsonc#secrets.required`. Whether the dev env
# contains 2 or 3 names depends on what the operator has seeded:
#
#   - Pre-#89 (legacy 2-name staged design): the dev env is seeded
#     with `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` + `MY_WEB_2026_CONSUMER_API_KEY`
#     (required) plus `BETTER_AUTH_SECRETS` (extra key kept around
#     so the primary path's injected set resembles the eventual
#     versioned prod form). The primary path therefore sees 3 names.
#   - Post-#89 (versioned 2-name flip): `secrets.required` is
#     renamed to `BETTER_AUTH_SECRETS` + `MY_WEB_2026_CONSUMER_API_KEY`;
#     `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` becomes a legacy optional outside the
#     required set. The dev env may or may not still contain it.
#
# Operator prerequisite: be logged in via `pnpm exec infisical login`
# once; the CLI caches the access token under `~/.infisical/`.
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fallback path: `pnpm run generate:dev-vars`  (REST → `.dev.vars`)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# When the Infisical CLI (`infisical` binary) is unavailable on the
# workstation — but the self-hosted Infisical API at
# `https://secrets.rebuildup.dev` is reachable AND a currently valid
# `INFISICAL_TOKEN` is exported — the fallback script
# `scripts/generate-dev-vars.mjs` fetches secrets via the documented
# Infisical API:
#
#   GET /api/v3/secrets/raw?workspaceId={...}&environment=dev&viewSecretValue=true
#
# and writes them to the gitignored `.dev.vars` (NOT this file) with
# mode `0o600` (atomic via temp + rename, with rollback on failure).
# The set it pulls is **constrained to
# `wrangler.jsonc#secrets.required`** — anything else in the Infisical
# dev env is silently ignored.
#
# IMPORTANT: the fallback ALWAYS mirrors exactly
# `wrangler.jsonc#secrets.required`. It does NOT widen the set to
# match the primary path's full dev env. Consequently:
#
#   - Pre-#89 (legacy 2-name staged design): fallback writes
#     `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` + `MY_WEB_2026_CONSUMER_API_KEY` only.
#   - Post-#89 (versioned 2-name flip, Issue #89): the required
#     array is renamed to `BETTER_AUTH_SECRETS` +
#     `MY_WEB_2026_CONSUMER_API_KEY`; the fallback continues to
#     mirror `secrets.required` automatically (no script change
#     needed — `secrets.required` is the source of truth) and
#     therefore writes the versioned 2-name set. It does NOT
#     become a 3-name set, and `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` (legacy
#     optional) is not materialised by the fallback.
#
# The fallback boundary is intentionally narrow: it requires
# network access to the Infisical API and a non-expired
# `INFISICAL_TOKEN`. It is NOT an offline path and it CANNOT work
# with an expired token. Operators who find themselves offline
# or token-less must use the primary `pnpm dev` path once those
# preconditions are restored.
#
# Required env for the fallback:
#   INFISICAL_TOKEN  short-lived operator token
# Optional:
#   INFISICAL_API_URL  default https://secrets.rebuildup.dev
# Usage:
#   pnpm run generate:dev-vars           # default env (dev)
#   pnpm run generate:dev-vars -- --env=dev
#   pnpm run generate:dev-vars -- --dry-run    # print plan only
#
# After running, `pnpm dev` (still wrapped through `_run-dev.mjs`)
# will simply pass the secrets in directly — but `wrangler dev` also
# reads the gitignored `.dev.vars` natively if present, so the
# fallback exists for non-Vite surfaces (e.g. ad-hoc
# `pnpm exec wrangler dev` during a debugging session).
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secret names (ADR-0015 §9 staged design)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The local dev contract is governed by
# `wrangler.jsonc#secrets.required`. The names currently in that
# array are listed below; this table documents their roles, not
# a fixed contract — the array is the source of truth.
#
#       ┌─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┐
#       │ Name                        │ Why                             │
#       ├─────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤
#       │ BETTER_AUTH_SECRET          │ legacy single signing key       │
#       │                             │ (Better Auth 1.5+ accepts this; │
#       │                             │ pre-#89 listed in               │
#       │                             │ `secrets.required`. Post-#89    │
#       │                             │ it remains a legacy optional    │
#       │                             │ OUTSIDE `secrets.required` and  │
#       │                             │ is no longer materialised by    │
#       │                             │ the fallback)                   │
#       ├─────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤
#       │ BETTER_AUTH_SECRETS         │ versioned form (Better Auth     │
#       │                             │ 1.5+, format `1:<hex>`). Post-  │
#       │                             │ #89 this REPLACES               │
#       │                             │ `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` in         │
#       │                             │ `secrets.required`. The dev env │
#       │                             │ may also carry this key today   │
#       │                             │ (pre-#89) so the primary path's │
#       │                             │ injected set resembles the      │
#       │                             │ eventual prod form. The         │
#       │                             │ fallback writes it only after    │
#       │                             │ #89                             │
#       ├─────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤
#       │ MY_WEB_2026_CONSUMER_API_KEY│ home-self-consumption API key   │
#       │                             │ (ADR-0011). Listed in           │
#       │                             │ `secrets.required` pre- and     │
#       │                             │ post-#89. Local dev: random;    │
#       │                             │ production: hashed in D1 via    │
#       │                             │ `ensure-home-api-key.mjs`       │
#       └─────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────┘
#
# Do NOT edit this file by hand. It is documentation of the
# secret-name contract — the canonical SoT is
# `wrangler.jsonc#secrets.required`. `pnpm run generate:dev-vars`
# does not overwrite this file; it writes the gitignored
# `.dev.vars` next to it. The real `.dev.vars` is gitignored and
# must never be committed.

# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="redacted-by-infisical-fallback"
# MY_WEB_2026_CONSUMER_API_KEY="mk_home_redacted-by-infisical-fallback"
# NOTE: this is a documentation template only — these lines are
# NEVER written to disk by `generate:dev-vars`. They illustrate
# the legacy 2-name set as it appears in `wrangler.jsonc#secrets.required`
# today; after #89 (Issue #89 versioned 2-name flip) the first
# line above becomes `BETTER_AUTH_SECRETS="..."` and the legacy
# `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` line falls out of `secrets.required`.
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local API mock layer (Issue #166)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When designing UI against canned data — for example, when the local
# D1 is empty or the home widget needs to be screenshotted without a
# real session — set `LOCAL_API_MODE=mock` in the gitignored `.dev.vars`
# to enable the design-verification layer at `src/http/mock/`. The mock
# handles 8 endpoints (auth.session / sign-in / sign-out, access.count /
# hit / principal, reactions/:slug / toggle). Endpoints outside that
# set (portfolio, keys, emoji-catalog, auth-invitations) fall through
# to the real handlers in mock mode.
#
# Unset / any value other than `mock` → production boundary unchanged.
# The env is intentionally NOT in `wrangler.jsonc#vars`; production
# deployments MUST NOT carry this var. The type augmentation is in
# `src/cloudflare/auth/env.d.ts`.
#
# # LOCAL_API_MODE="mock"
